WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:05.840
Phew! 2017 is coming to a close and this is now my fifth year reviewing a whole year of anime.

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:10.400
But before we jump into what 2017 did for anime, what happened in the rest of the world?

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:19.560
The eclipse happened for America, causing a nationwide purge of sight for people who took the advice of every possible outlet telling them not to stare directly at it as a fucking dare

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:25.260
This was swiftly followed by hallucinations of a giant man in black armor with a massive sword shouting angrily at the sky.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:30.640
It was a tough year for tragic events; stories of sexual harassment coming to light and North Korean threat ever stronger

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:36.200
Which is no surprise that the biggest group of people causing us to lose faith in humanity this year was 'Rick and Morty' fans

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:41.420
by completely losing their shit, caused by massive outrage over a bit of teriyaki sauce mixed with ketchup.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:48.500
And of course the fidget spinner craze took over the world, showing the terrifying power of having a mildly satisfying feeling in your hands.

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:52.960
In response, the World Health Organization advised people to start take up smoking instead,

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:57.660
with new research coming to light suggesting you would pose a significantly less risk to cancer

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:02.360
But of course we're here to talk about the last year in anime and everything that happened in our community

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:05.320
Of course I won't be able to cover everything, but I will do my best

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:13.480
So as we roll back the clock to Winter, the community found some love during the cold months to warm our icy hearts in DreamWork's highly acclaimed

00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:16.340
How to Train Your Dragon

00:01:16.340 --> 00:01:17.020
How to Train Your Dragon Waifu

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:26.280
♪ Aozora no Rhapsody (青空のラプソディ) by fhána ♪

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:34.440
This year started off with some wholesome goodness as 'Miss Kobayashi's Maid Dragon' proved to us that the king of cute still firmly remains in Kyoto Animation's hands.

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:36.740
It was the show that grabbed the community for some reason

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:39.380
I mean, I don't know what's so great about a dragon in the maid outfit.

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:43.060
I mean sure she's cute and all but I don't really see why the community would go crazy about this

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:44.020
Kanna: 'Oooh'

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:47.620
*Sounds of IT'S SO CUTE D'AWWWWWWWWWW-*

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:53.320
A lonely adult working woman actually one day finds a dragon at her doorstep who enthusiastically offers to be her maid.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:57.360
And thus we follow the daily life of Kobayashi as along the way she meets an assortment of dragons

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:03.280
who all end up growing a close bond to her, wanting to stay by her side of course making her true name Miss Kobayashi...

00:02:03.900 --> 00:02:06.720
Stormborn of House Targaryen,  Mother of Dragons, Breaker of Chains

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:15.340
Beyond this, it was just a heartwarming tale about family values and how we can find family with the people we meet and spend time with, even if those bonds aren't made by blood.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:20.900
But let's be real here, we all know the true reason we watched the show as Kanna's cuteness dominated the community for that season.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:26.560
Clips and gifs flooded all of social media with carnosine, signifying the next level of cute animal videos

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:31.700
Detailing these terrifying ancient mythical creatures becoming domesticated for our viewing pleasure

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.060
Oh bububububu

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:35.660
Who can destroy the world to bring about the apocalypse?

00:02:35.660 --> 00:02:38.220
Yes, you can! Yes you can!

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:39.100
Ooo boo boo boo boo boo boo

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:44.580
On a sidenote, the official music video for the OP is one of the most unintentionally entertaining things to come out of this,

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:49.360
just because this guitarist is the epitome of that unimpressed normie friend you see at anime conventions.

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:52.740
Being forced into doing this weird weeb shit that he doesn't get

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:58.600
In the rest of the Winter, 'Fuuka' gave an anime adaptation for a manga that caused major controversy for its preexisting fans

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:03.520
by completely changing major plot points, only to diverge entirely by the second half of the show.

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:09.320
While many argued the anime was doomed from the beginning without enough episodes to properly conclude the events laid out in the beginning of the manga,

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:13.100
It was clear that either way the adaptation really got hit by a truck.

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:15.640
Oh wait, no it fucking didn't.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:23.540
After much anticipation from his highly successful OVA, Studio Trigger finally debuted the first full season of 'Boku no Chibi Potter Academia'

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:29.720
Despite the mostly positive reception it received from viewers, and the hype had going for it, it failed to make a big impact on the community

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:37.100
marking the first time fans really felt the effect of the highly anticipated anime being held hostage behind the red bars of Netflix's prison

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:39.940
A pattern that would soon be felt more as the year went by.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:47.940
'Youjo Senki' gave us another contender for loli of the season with the story of a middle-aged man trapped in the body of a nine year old girl during an alternate reality World War One.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:57.140
Yes, Kanna has her work cut out as she may have her adorable eating scenes, but how can she possibly compete... with... the precious smile...

00:03:57.140 --> 00:04:00.480
of Crazy-Rocket-Loli Hitler murdering hundreds of soldiers

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:03.060
CUTE!

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:09.820
'Rakugo Shinjuu' got another season; giving me a chance to redeem myself from the endless comments I got for missing this masterpiece in last year's run down

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:12.700
So now that I've been given this chance I can safely say that

00:04:12.700 --> 00:04:17.520
'Masamune-Kun’s Revenge' was a tsundere harem junk food that I actually enjoyed a lot.

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:24.720
A tale about an overly-confident, narcissistic asshole trying to get revenge over a stoic tsundere bitch who rejects them ages ago because he was fat.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:30.860
Which sounds cheesy and dumb, and was cheesy and dumb, but somehow ended up being the perfect popcorn and seinen rom-com.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:39.500
Okay, fine, I'll talk about 'Rakugo,' past the first season's somewhat disconnected 45 minutes slow burn over first episode that turns me and a lot of people off initially

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:47.740
'Rakugo' demonstrates some of the best that anime has to offer. It's a beautiful character driven story told through Rakugo, the not so well known art form that it is

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:54.120
but the character surrounding this concept are so well fleshed out and compelling, that it was simply a joy to experience life from their shoes

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:58.620
and this season followed suit from the first to definitely become one of the contenders of anime of the year

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:04.140
'Handshakers' gave us a highly ambitious car crash about a group of kids who get superpowers by holding hands.

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:06.820
And if that sounds bad to you, don't worry.

00:05:06.820 --> 00:05:08.580
That was the best part of the show.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:12.880
Yes, if the audience weren't put off by enough excessive camera movements to induce motion sickness,

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:18.360
Then its visual style was so ugly, I now have a permanent phobia of badly animated CG chains.

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:22.580
Our favorite lovable cast of idiots returned for another season in 'Konosuba 2'

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:29.420
Giving us the fun, stupid fantasy adventures that is basically the animated experience of playing Dungeons &amp; Dragons with a group of drunk pissheads.

00:05:29.420 --> 00:05:36.540
'Scum’s Wish' gave us a genre about a group of scummy people being scummy with each other because everyone's in a relationship where they'd rather be with someone else

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:44.480
That's right, as an anime set in Cuckfield where it's always NTR o'clock; so of course with such a recipe, It was only ever going to end one way

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:48.220
Yep, it' the return of everyone's favorite old friend. If you he happy happy clap your hands and

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:51.340
♪ If you're happy, happy, happy, clap your hands ♪

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:57.120
And finally the surprise hit of the season came with 'Kemono Friends' which took Japan by storm

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:01.800
With its depiction of cute little anthropomorphized anime girls, to which my first thought was

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:03.860
"Wow, I fucking wonder why"

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:08.360
But the series turned out to be a light-hearted original experience for anime that no one expected.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:15.420
Fueled by the fact that during a promotional run at a zoo, one of the cardboard cutouts called the affection of a lone penguin, Grape-Kun

00:06:15.420 --> 00:06:19.840
Yes the story of Grape-Kun and his waifu exploded on the internet and how could it not ?

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:25.680
it's fucking adorable! As of course Usenet that has never had any obsession with any animal ever before

00:06:25.680 --> 00:06:29.540
Unfortunately, a few months later, Grape-Kun did pass away

00:06:29.540 --> 00:06:39.040
And of course the anime community mourned at the loss of one of our own showing that our love for waifus transcends gender, belief, and species.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:43.960
Rest in peace Grape-Kun. Jesus may have died for our sins

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:47.600
but Grape-Kun died for our waifus.

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:56.640
As Spring rolled around there was much anticipation in the air as two of the hottest properties of the last few years were back and vying for the top spot in the Battle of Season Twos.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:04.800
One was the old king, finally back after many years of anticipation; and the other was the new kid on the block continuing to make a name for themselves in this new era

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:07.760
That's right, the boys were back in town.

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:13.820
♪ The Boys Are Back In Town ♪

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:18.140
After four years of waiting, 'Attack on Titan' returned to us and it was almost like it never left

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:22.440
Titans once again walked the line of pants-shittingly terrifying to pants-shittingly stupid,

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:26.000
Eren was still a loud uptight fuck who can't stop failing a life and once again

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:31.580
We were given an opening that everyone thinks they can sing, even though they only literally know one word

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:37.880
Tonally however, this season was far different from the previous one, focusing more on mystery and horror than all out action and hype.

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:45.280
But despite being the sequel to one of the hottest anime properties of all the time the hype surrounding it was nowhere near what it was during its peak in season one.

00:07:45.280 --> 00:07:53.620
Showing us that waiting for years probably wasn't the best thing to do as this new seasonal anime climate has given the community a collective memory that lasts about three and a half days

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:59.760
While undoubtedly it was still popular, the series that rose up to take the spotlight for the community was 'My Hero Academia'

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:06.020
Though the first season was highly loved by Shonen fans, it was this season that really catapulted it into sky-high popularity.

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:09.820
Most likely for its longer run, the absolute hype surrounding his take on its

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:11.440
T-T-T-T-T

00:08:11.440 --> 00:08:12.080
TO

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:12.780
TOU

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:13.540
TOUR

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:19.880
... "structured series of individual fights" arc. And for hosting one of the standout fights in the year for anime.

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:21.140
That's right:

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:24.820
'Boku no Hero Academia' versus 'My Hero Academia'

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:26.740
"IT'S MY HERO ACADEMIA!"

00:08:26.740 --> 00:08:29.140
"IT'S BOKU NO HERO ACADEMIA!"

00:08:29.140 --> 00:08:31.640
"STOP TRYING TO BE JAPANESE, YOU WEEB!"

00:08:31.640 --> 00:08:33.340
"IT JUST ROLLS OFF THE TONGUE BETTER"

00:08:33.340 --> 00:08:35.360
"Why can't we just call it Hero Aca?!"

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:37.560
"Well, I call it Macadamia!"

00:08:41.760 --> 00:08:43.560
*in the distance*
"What is wrong with you?"

00:08:43.560 --> 00:08:49.060
I have nothing more to add over the things I've said and have been saying since last year's recap as it just continues to be a

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:52.860
very high-quality shonen action show, staying true to us John Roos roots

00:08:52.860 --> 00:08:55.700
Ultimately, which title won The Battle Season Twos?

00:08:55.700 --> 00:09:00.740
Well, there's only one way we can settle this. What you really want me to bring it back one last time?

00:09:00.780 --> 00:09:01.720
fine.

00:09:09.020 --> 00:09:13.520
STRUCTURED SERIES OF INDIVIDUAL FIGHTS ARRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRC!

00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:19.380
In the rest of the season, 'King's Avatar' gave China's first attempt at giving the world an eSports anime that was less an eSports anime

00:09:19.380 --> 00:09:26.040
and more an ex-pro making a bunch of new friends by dicking about in bronze in 'Anime Smurfing: The Dyrus Chronicles'

00:09:26.040 --> 00:09:30.540
'Akashic Records of I Thought We'd Grown Out of the Battle Harem Magic Highschool Phase By Now' anime

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:37.160
Gave us a Magic High School where the most magical thing was how they confused the stripper outfit for a school uniform, as only the girls seemingly need to wear it.

00:09:37.160 --> 00:09:44.040
It's degrading, objectifying, and I am so horrified that I want to meet the genius who approved this

00:09:44.040 --> 00:09:45.920
Seriously who thought of this? I need to shake his hand.

00:09:45.920 --> 00:09:50.660
Roy: "All female officers will be required to wear TINY MINISKIRTS"

00:09:50.660 --> 00:09:54.860
We got a continuation to our favorite loud yellow haired ninja that everyone expected to suck,

00:09:54.860 --> 00:10:01.480
but actually turned out to be a great homage to what made the original anime appeal to us in the first place while tackling it in a new enough way to keep it fresh

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:04.960
In 'Naruto's Son: Child of Boruto's Dad'

00:10:04.960 --> 00:10:11.560
The suffering continued as 'Berzerk 2017' continued kicking fans while they were down who was still left an agony from last year thinking

00:10:11.560 --> 00:10:14.600
"Well at least there's no way it can look any worse than 'Berzerk 2016'

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:16.500
OH GOD, WHAT HAVE YOU DONE?!

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:23.140
"Well I don't get why you guys are complaining about I mean it's stupid"

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.820
"Hey hey, hold mfmphhhmp"

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:26.300
*squish*

00:10:26.300 --> 00:10:34.040
The sleeper it of the season was 'Tsuki ga Kirei,' a grounded portrayal of teenage Relationships that unfortunately got swept under the masses of big shows this season.

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:40.360
one of the most realistic takes of adolescent romance I have seen recently that breaks all the bullshit conventions you'd normally see in anime.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:44.460
Like no over dramatic melodrama, parents are actually present,

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:48.880
and they even show the superpower granted only to us introverts

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:51.340
communication through awkward silences

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:58.380
*cries* I know the feel, bro!

00:10:58.400 --> 00:11:06.340
Meta was taken to a whole new level as 'Re:Creators' gave us a show about anime and game characters being transported to the real world and meeting their creators

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:12.460
Yes, we had budget Saber meeting her author, should-have-been-a-'Monogatari'-villain versus should-have-been-a-'JoJo'-character

00:11:12.460 --> 00:11:17.560
and Madoka Magica causing collateral damage with her completely OP friendship powers

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:21.180
God, I love this fucking show!

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:26.260
The only thing missing was for an Isekai character to be transported to their world where he would get confused thinking he was transported back to his homeworld.

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:31.400
'Kado: The Right Answer' gave us some interesting thought experiment of how easy it would be to advance the human race

00:11:31.400 --> 00:11:35.860
given new technology that could give us Infinite resources and understanding of our universe

00:11:35.860 --> 00:11:39.140
While interesting, it was obviously very unrealistic as in reality

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:48.160
It would never be this stupidly difficult to unite the human race under a technology that everyone would be able to use equally without being controlled by people for their own gain.

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:50.880
Ha. Ah ha ha ha. Ah ha ha ha ha ha HA

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:57.380
'Sword Oratoria: Is It Wrong to Pick Up Girls in a Dungeon On The Side' gave us a side story to 'Danmachi' featuring not Hestia

00:11:57.380 --> 00:12:01.320
But even this season had competitions for most overly convoluted title based on a light novel as

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:06.180
'What do you do at the end of the world? Are you busy? Will you save us? Question Marks Included'

00:12:06.180 --> 00:12:09.760
attempted it's best to go for the word count limit for new anime titles MAL.

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:17.940
And finally, 'Eromanga Sensei' exploded onto the scene, giving us the harem incest baits loli fanservice absolutely none of us asked for.

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:20.240
But we all watched anyway.

00:12:20.240 --> 00:12:26.060
Of course, following from 'Oreimo' you would have to do something special to make waves in the community and that it certainly did.

00:12:26.060 --> 00:12:32.760
Combining elements of the absolute lowest paths of anime into one show and taking it just that level beyond!

00:12:32.760 --> 00:12:35.080
It was tasteless, It was pandering

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:37.480
It was downright questionably illegal

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:44.540
And just when you think it couldn't get any lower, it asked you to hold his beer while it jumps in the dumpster to take us further below.

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:57.980
Despite the fact it was an absolutely awful show, we just couldn't stop watching before somehow enjoying the experience

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:01.420
Then accepting it for the awful garbage that it was.

00:13:01.420 --> 00:13:04.500
And for better, or worse, this year would not have been the same without it

00:13:04.500 --> 00:13:09.520
Thank you 'Eromanga Sensei' for providing us with such entertainment over the years and an endless well of memes.

00:13:09.520 --> 00:13:14.140
Thank you for uniting us and making us realize that we are all just a bunch of the degenerates at heart!

00:13:14.140 --> 00:13:18.160
Goodbye, respectable taste in anime! 
Hello, FBI registering!

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:23.320
The otaku fandom has spoken again and the final answer to the rest of the world is that

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:24.180
ANIME

00:13:24.180 --> 00:13:24.840
ANIME IS

00:13:24.840 --> 00:13:26.260
ANIME IS TRASH!

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:27.080
ANIME IS TRASH! AND

00:13:27.080 --> 00:13:27.980
ANIME IS TRASH! AND SO

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:28.940
ANIME IS TRASH! AND SO ARE

00:13:28.940 --> 00:13:31.680
ANIME IS TRASH! AND SO ARE WE!

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:32.980
See you in part 2.

00:13:34.140 --> 00:13:40.020
Hey guys, I hope you enjoyed the video if you would like to check out all the previous anime year reviews click on this playlist here.

00:13:40.020 --> 00:13:43.260
Just to check out just how much anime has changed in the last five years

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:48.260
this is my fifth year doing it and if part two is out the link will be right over the video I've put here as a placeholder.

00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:54.400
Which should hopefully be in a few days. Anyway, that's it for me. I will see you guys later.

